Got it 👍
You want the error message in ValidatePaths to also show where the file was last moved / renamed by the archive sub (the SRC path), so when something fails you immediately know which file and from where caused the problem.

Right now, the archive routine only Debug.Prints the SRC/DST, so the Validate sub has no idea about it.

✅ Clean & safe way to do this

Use a global variable to store the last archive source path, then show it in the error MsgBox.


---

1️⃣ Add a PUBLIC variable (very important)

Put this at the very top of a standard module (above all Subs):

Public gLastArchiveSRC As String

This makes the value accessible anywhere (including ValidatePaths).


---

2️⃣ Update ArchiveExistingByPrefix to capture SRC

Modify your archive sub like this (only a small change 👇):

Sub ArchiveExistingByPrefix(srcFolder As String, archiveFolder As String, prefix6 As String)
    Dim f As String
    Dim timeStamp As String

    timeStamp = Format(Now, "mmddyyyy_hhmmss")

    f = Dir(srcFolder & prefix6 & "*.xls*")

    Do While f <> ""
        gLastArchiveSRC = srcFolder & f   ' <<< STORE SRC PATH

        Name srcFolder & f As archiveFolder & _
             Left(f, InStrRev(f, ".") - 1) & "_" & timeStamp & Mid(f, InStrRev(f, "."))

        f = Dir
    Loop
End Sub

Now every time an archive happens, the exact source file path is remembered.


---

3️⃣ Enhance the ERROR MsgBox in ValidatePaths

Replace this part:

If Err.Number <> 0 Then
    MsgBox "Process ended with error: " & Err.Description, vbExclamation
    Exit Sub
End If

🔁 With this upgraded version:

If Err.Number <> 0 Then
    Dim msg As String

    msg = "Process ended with error:" & vbCrLf & _
          Err.Description

    If gLastArchiveSRC <> "" Then
        msg = msg & vbCrLf & vbCrLf & _
              "Source file before archive:" & vbCrLf & _
              gLastArchiveSRC
    End If

    MsgBox msg, vbCritical
    Exit Sub
End If


